  "_notes": [
    "Ground truth for the W3C Before and After Demonstration (BAD) 'before' pages. Never edit a label to make a result look better.",
    "Source: the W3C evaluation report for each page (the report URL on each page). Every issue here is a success criterion the report marks Fail, at Level A or AA. The reports are criterion-level, not element-level, so scoring matches a finding to a label by (url, wcag).",
    "BAD targets WCAG 2.0; every criterion listed also exists at the same level in WCAG 2.1.",
    "in_scope: true if one of the agent's v1 checks (an axe rule, or alt text quality, link text meaning, heading structure, label clarity) can see the criterion. Out-of-scope issues need behavioural or cross-page testing (keyboard, focus, layout-table reading order, consistency across pages). Report recall over in_scope issues, and over all issues.",
    "The reports list only what W3C's evaluator found. A finding on a criterion not listed here counts against precision even if it is arguably real; do not add labels to compensate.",
    "page_sha256 / report_sha256 hash the HTML as retrieved on 2026-11-10 so drift in the live pages can be detected.",
    "detectable_by and in_scope are the only fields not taken from the reports; they describe the agent, not the page."
